   "body": "Adversarial review round 1, Opus 5.5 (read-only sub-agent), verbatim:\n\n**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5): REQUEST CHANGES** — head 31e3e18\n\n1. **High**: `Packages/HFRKit/Tests/HFRParsingTests/Forms/HopResponseParserTests.swift:7`. The new `editRightsRefusal` test makes the struct body 255 lines, over the 250-line limit, so `swiftlint lint --strict` reports `type_body_length` as an error. CI runs exactly that command (`ci.yml:28`, swiftlint 0.65.1), so the SwiftLint job will fail. I ran SwiftLint 0.65.1 in strict mode on both trees: the base is clean, this head fails. Fix: move the test into its own `@Suite` struct, for example next to `HopResponseAlertTests` and `HopResponsePollVoteTests`. Do not add a disable comment.\n2. **Medium**: the docs are stale (L08/L21).\n   - `docs/lots/LOT-037-hop-response-classifier.md:31-44`: the behaviour table is the classifier's contract and has no row for the new rule (a link-less `.hop` containing \"pas les droits pour éditer\", `.write` only → `rejected`, `W440c`).\n   - `docs/lots/LOT-037-hop-response-classifier.md:77-78`: the \"Pending capture\" list should mention the new rule.\n   - `docs/lots/LOT-052-mpstorage-transport.md:86-88`: still says `save` reports `posting(.unconfirmed(.unrecognizedAnswer))` and that \"`rejected` is #756\".\n   - Fix: add the table row and update the LOT-052 sentence.\n3. **Low**: `HopResponseParser.swift:18` (`Context.write` doc) still says only that a `.hop` with a link or input is a refusal. Mention the `W440c` sentence there.\n4. **Detail**: `HopResponseParser.swift:82` and `HFR-PROTOCOL.md:529` say \"692 captures\". That counts every file in `captures/`. Only 282 are HTML pages, which is what the sweep covers. Say \"282 HTML captures\".\n\n**Verified**\n- Re-swept every HTML fixture under `Tests/` and `App/` with my own parser. Fifteen pages have a link-less `.hop` without \"avec succès\": R08-1, R08-3, R50a, R70a-d (\"Identifiants invalides !\"), R71a/b, W01, W01b, W03, W42, W45 and W440c. W440c is the only write refusal among them.\n- \"pas les droits\" occurs only in W440c. No other \"droits\" sentence appears in any `.hop`. The sentence match is justified.\n- Checked all callers of `classify` under `.write`: SessionRefreshFlow (needs `message == nil`), PostingFlow form/confirmation, TopicSearchFlow, TopicFlagFlow, DeletePrivateMessageFlow. None can misfire. A success cannot match, because the negation filter already rejects \"pas\". `.pollVote`, `.alertSubmit` and `.alertPrepare` are unchanged.\n- `swift test --filter \"HopResponseParserTests|MPStorageTransportWriteTests|PostingFlow\"`: 41 passed. With the base `HopResponseParser.swift` restored, both new or updated tests fail. The success sweep stays green.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
