   "body": "Adversarial review round 2, Opus 5.5 (read-only sub-agent), verbatim:\n\n**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5): APPROVE**, head ac428ca\n\nMy verdict is APPROVE. The parser change is narrow: it applies under `.write` only, after the link/input branch, and before the success guard. W17c and the success sweeps are unchanged. Both tests fail without the Sources change. I found three Low items; none blocks the merge.\n\n1. **Low**, `HopResponseParser.swift:83` and `docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md:529`: the corpus claim lists the other link-less `.hop` pages as \"lists, the search wait page, login and poll pages\". My sweep of the 282 HTML captures also finds `R70a`-`R70d` (\"Identifiants invalides !\") and `R71a`/`R71b` (\"Mot de passe incorrect !\"). Both are link-less and negative. They are GET pages, so \"no other link-less write refusal\" still holds, but someone re-checking the claim against the corpus would find these pages missing from the list. Fix: add \"stale-session/profile pages (`R70*`, `R71*`)\" to both places, as the PR body already does.\n2. **Low**, PR body: two statements do not match the diff.\n   - It names `HopResponseParserTests.editRightsRefusal`, but the tests are `HopResponseEditRefusalTests.rejectedUnderWrite` and `HopResponseEditRefusalTests.otherContextsUnchanged`.\n   - It says the sweep covered \"all 692 captures\", while the docs say 282 HTML captures. Fixture files total 913 and capture `.html` files 282.\n   Fix: edit the body. This needs no push.\n3. **Detail**, `HopResponseEditRefusalTests.swift:19`: only `.alertPrepare` is checked. `.pollVote` and `.alertSubmit` are not checked, though the code gates them the same way. Optional.\n\n**Verified**\n- Worktree at ac428ca.\n- `swiftlint lint --strict` on the three touched Swift files: 0 violations.\n- `swift test --filter 'HopResponse|MPStorageTransportWrite'`: 64 tests passed.\n- Mutation test: with the `isRightsRefusal` branch turned off, `rejectedUnderWrite` and `anotherAccountsMessageIsNotASuccess` fail.\n- Independent Python sweep of every link-less `.hop` in the 282 HTML captures: `W440c` is the only write refusal.\n- Grep for stale wording about \"unrecognized/unconfirmed\" for `W440c`: none left in the docs or the tests (LOT-037, LOT-052, HFR-PROTOCOL, HopResponseParserTests:174).\n- No ledger entry is needed: no legacy fix, no GAP row.\n\nAuthor's note: item 2 fixed in the PR body. Items 1 and 3 are Low and optional; not pushed, to spare a CI run on an approved head (the R70/R71 pages are already in the PR body's list and are GET pages).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
